i18n="annual.copy.8305f2aab5f1">Period convention and original labels</summary><p>${annualTextHTML(d.anchor.classification)} ${localizedText("annual.anchor.firstPeriod",{period:d.ticker==='KEYS'?annualLabel(d.anchor.firstModeledPeriod):d.anchor.firstModeledPeriod})} ${annualTextHTML(d.anchor.fiscalCalendarCaution||'Calendar-year periods.')}</p>${table('Original source period labels',['Model year','Original period'],d.annual.map(r=>[localizedText('annual.year',{year:r.year}),`<span data-original-source title="${esc(r.period)}">${annualTextHTML(r.period)}</span>`]))}<p data-i18n="annual.copy.711cf2ffaa08">Investment includes capital spending less D&amp;A and operating working-capital / lease effects where separately modeled.</p></details><details class="terminal-editor"><summary data-terminal-summary>${localizedText("annual.terminal.summary",{growth:pct(d.terminal.growth),wacc:pct(d.terminal.wacc)})}</summary><div class="research-field-grid">${tfields.map(([key,label])=>`<label>${annualTextHTML(label)}${input(key,d.terminal[key],label,{group:'terminal',scale:100})}</label>`).join('')}</div></details><p class="micro" data-i18n="annual.copy.43e657da99e2">Capital-component reconciliations describe the original researched path. After editing investment or margin, check the source economics again; the model does not manufacture a replacement gross-capex budget.</p></section>
 <details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing"><summary data-i18n="annual.copy.39ecbd08229e">Valuation date and partial-year cash flow</summary>${reviewedStubHTML(d,{detail:true})}<label for="research-timing-mode" data-i18n="annual.copy.8db36da76efa">Value basis</label><select id="research-timing-mode" data-research-select="timing"><option value="origin" ${d.timing?.mode==='origin'?'selected':''} data-i18n="annual.copy.d3b1605ba809">Forecast-origin value · no timing assumption</option><option value="as-of-scenario" ${d.timing?.mode==='as-of-scenario'?'selected':''} data-i18n="annual.copy.84187f695342">Explicit as-of timing scenario</option></select><p>${annualTextHTML(d.ticker==='MRVL'?MRVL_MESSAGES.note[0]:d.ticker==='SNPS'?SNPS_STUB_NOTE:d.openingStub?CDNS_STUB_NOTE:forecastAnchor?'The revenue base is management’s FY2026 forecast. It is not an observed TTM period. The remaining October 17–December 31 FCFF must be added and the whole future stream discounted over the extra stub interval.':'The annual stream begins at the reported anchor. An October value must remove already-elapsed FCFF before discounting the remaining stream from October.')}</p><div class="research-field-grid"><label><span data-i18n="annual.copy.ddef9e5a6ef4">Scenario date</span><input id="research-asof" type="date" value="${esc(d.timing?.asOf||'2026-10-17')}" data-research-text="asOf" min="2026-10-17"></label><label>${localizedText('annual.timing.millions',{label:annualLabel(forecastAnchor?'Remaining pre-origin FCFF':'Already-elapsed first-year FCFF')})}${input('stubFCFF',d.timing?.stubFCFF,forecastAnchor?'Remaining pre-origin FCFF':'Already elapsed FCFF',{group:'timing'})}</label>${forecastAnchor||d.ticker==='SNPS'?`<label>${localizedText('annual.timing.stubRate')}${input('stubDiscountRate',d.timing?.stubDiscountRate,'Stub discount rate percent',{group:'timing',scale:100})}</label>`:''}</div><label for="research-stub-reason" data-i18n="annual.copy.8626ad6f42a0">Source or explicit timing assumption</label><textarea id="research-stub-reason" rows="3" data-research-text="reason">${esc(d.timing?.reason||'')}</textarea><p class="micro" data-i18n="annual.copy.1ef724ceedd8">Blank stays unknown. Entering zero is a substantive assumption and needs an explanation. Calendar proration, if chosen, is an analyst assumption; no realized cash flow is inferred. Dated equity-bridge balances need their own roll-forward.</p></details>
 <details class="research-card" data-annual-section="differences"><summary data-i18n="annual.copy.769b1416b333">How Year-by-year differs from Guided</summary><p data-i18n="annual.copy.42226c5b3513">Guided generates a path from broad assumptions. Year-by-year exposes individual annual inputs. Both use discounted cash flow, but their assumption paths are separate and are not synchronized. These annual research cases use reviewed company-specific revenue and margin schedules, direct annual investment, company-specific revenue-growth horizons and dated claim adjustments. Those changes can materially change value without any stock-price target.</p><p data-i18n="annual.copy.041d76567b5b">MU keeps investing during declining sales. AAOI and NBIS start from explicitly forecast FY2026 anchors. AMZN and GOOG use capital/funding reconciliations. Terminal transitions and uncertainty are shown separately rather than hidden in a smooth curve.</p><p class="micro" data-i18n="annual.copy.9df79ba38040">Annual Monte Carlo uses the explicit investment-response policy selected in its controls. The complete preset includes explicit company-specific uncertainty assumptions. Fixed zero-offset stresses reproduce the deterministic case; uncertainty and parameter relationships remain analyst judgments. The Guided simulation remains separate.</p></details>`;
 // CDNS cannot roll its reviewed source stub to another valuation date. Retain
 // saved timing values for recovery/export, but do not offer unusable controls.
 if(d.ticker==='KEYS')return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,()=>`<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing"><summary>${annualTextHTML('Valuation date and partial-year cash flow')}</summary><p>${annualTextHTML(KEYS_MESSAGES.scope[0])}</p></details>`);
 if(d.ticker==='ARM')return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,()=>`<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing"><summary>${annualTextHTML('Valuation date and partial-year cash flow')}</summary><p>${annualTextHTML(ARM_MESSAGES.scope[0])}</p></details>`);
 if(d.ticker==='SNDK')return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,()=>`<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing"><summary>${annualTextHTML('Valuation date and partial-year cash flow')}</summary><p>${annualTextHTML(SNDK_MESSAGES.scope[0])}</p></details>`);
 if(d.ticker==='CRDO')return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,()=>`<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing"><summary>${annualTextHTML('Valuation date and partial-year cash flow')}</summary><p>${annualTextHTML('CRDO values the remaining fiscal stub from October 18, 2026. October balances are estimates; changing the valuation date requires a newly reviewed operating and capital bridge.')}</p></details>`);
 if(!d.openingStub)return html;
 if(d.ticker==='SNPS')return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,(_,start,body,end)=>start+body.replace('</summary>',`</summary><p id="snps-timing-help" class="research-warning">${annualTextHTML('This dated case uses a fixed fiscal Q4 stub; a new valuation date needs a reviewed operating and capital bridge.')}</p>`).replace('value="as-of-scenario"','value="as-of-scenario" disabled').replace(/<(input|textarea) /g,'<$1 disabled aria-describedby="snps-timing-help" ')+end);
 return html.replace(/(<details class="research-card" data-annual-section="timing">)([\s\S]*?)(<\/details>)/,(_,start,body,end)=>start+body.replace('</summary>',`</summary><p id="cdns-timing-help" class="research-warning">${annualTextHTML('This dated case uses a fixed H2 stub; a new valuation date needs a reviewed operating and capital bridge.')}</p>`).replace('value="as-of-scenario"','value="as-of-scenario" disabled').replace(/<(input|textarea) /g,'<$1 disabled aria-describedby="cdns-timing-help" ')+end);

}

